┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ 1) USER / CLIENT APP                                                       │
│    - Browser / mobile app / Postman / another service                      │
└──────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                               │
                               │ (A) User signs in
                               ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ 2) EXTERNAL IDP                                                            │
│    - Auth0 / Okta / Entra / Cognito                                        │
│    - Issues EXTERNAL OAuth/JWT token                                       │
└──────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                               │
                               │ (B) User calls Runtime with bearer token
                               ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ 3) AGENTCORE RUNTIME                                                       │
│                                                                             │
│   3a. RUNTIME INBOUND AUTH                                                  │
│       [AGENTCORE IDENTITY EXERCISED]                                        │
│       - Validates inbound JWT                                               │
│       - Confirms caller can access Runtime                                  │
│                                                                             │
│   3b. TOKEN EXCHANGE / INTERNAL TRUST SETUP                                 │
│       [AGENTCORE IDENTITY EXERCISED]                                        │
│       - Extracts USER identity from JWT                                     │
│       - Looks up RUNTIME WORKLOAD identity                                  │
│       - BINDS them together:                                                │
│           "This Runtime workload is acting on behalf of this user"          │
│       - Obtains WORKLOAD ACCESS TOKEN                                       │
│                                                                             │
│       Binding result conceptually:                                          │
│       {                                                                     │
│         user: "Lakshmi",                                                    │
│         workload: "Runtime-Agent-123",                                      │
│         permissions: [allowed tools/providers]                              │
│       }                                                                     │
│                                                                             │
│       IMPORTANT:                                                            │
│       - Workload Access Token is NOT the backend API token                  │
│       - It is for first-party AgentCore services only                       │
│       - Runtime automatically receives it during execution                  │
│                                                                             │
│   3c. AGENT EXECUTION                                                       │
│       - Runs agent logic / orchestration                                    │
│       - Decides a tool is needed                                            │
└──────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                               │
                               │ (C) Runtime code calls Gateway MCP endpoint
                               │
                               │ IMPORTANT:
                               │ - Your code chooses WHERE to call
                               │ - This call IMPLICITLY carries forward the
                               │   already-bound AgentCore context from 3b
                               │ - The MCP URL is the destination only;
                               │   AgentCore handles context propagation
                               ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ 4) AGENTCORE GATEWAY                                                       │
│                                                                             │
│   4a. GATEWAY INBOUND AUTH                                                  │
│       [AGENTCORE IDENTITY EXERCISED]                                        │
│       - Validates whoever is calling the Gateway                            │
│       - Protects Gateway as its own entry point                             │
│                                                                             │
│   4b. TOOL FACADE / MCP ENDPOINT                                            │
│       - Exposes tools through MCP                                           │
│       - Supports tools/list and tools/call                                  │
│                                                                             │
│   4c. GATEWAY OUTBOUND AUTH REQUEST                                         │
│       [AGENTCORE IDENTITY EXERCISED]                                        │
│       - Gateway uses the propagated internal AgentCore context              │
│       - Workload access token is applied automatically behind the scenes     │
│       - Identity uses that token/context to understand:                     │
│           • which workload is asking                                        │
│           • which user it is acting for                                     │
│           • what permissions apply                                          │
│                                                                             │
│       Example decision:                                                     │
│       "Can Runtime-Agent-123, acting for Lakshmi, use LoanAPI provider?"    │
│                                                                             │
│       - If allowed, Identity authorizes access to credentials               │
└──────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                               │
                               │ (D) If OAuth is needed, Identity uses the
                               │     configured credential provider / token
                               │     endpoint flow to get the REAL backend
                               │     API token
                               ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ 5) DOWNSTREAM AUTH SERVER / TOKEN ENDPOINT                                 │
│    - Returns ACTUAL OAuth access token for backend API                      │
│    - Different from the Workload Access Token                               │
└──────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                               │
                               │ (E) Real API token returned to Gateway
                               ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ 6) BACKEND TARGET                                                          │
│    - API / Lambda / SaaS / AWS service / MCP server                         │
│    - Gateway calls target using the REAL outbound credentials               │
└──────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                               │
                               │ (F) Response
                               ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ 7) RESPONSE PATH                                                           │
│    Backend Target → Gateway → Runtime → User                                │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
